+BUILD WITH CHANGES
+
+1. **P1 — The Live stage touches a listed defence and cannot be built as written in this run.** The plan explicitly changes `src/routes.ts`, which the security map classifies as a defence-bearing file, and “the live tool endpoint is unchanged” would let a Guide session execute the full Chat allowlist because `runTool` receives no `kind`. That contradicts the documented rule that `toolsFor(kind)` is an enforced boundary, not merely the list shown to the model. Move the Live route/tool work into a write-up for Greg. If later approved, bind tool calls and stored receipts to the journalled session’s effective kind and enforce that kind’s allowlist. The simplest interim spoken Guide would expose only browser-local `show_passage`, with no `/live-tool` calls. The greeting, command row, and reader-pressed CTA do not themselves alter `chat-commands.ts`’s model-action defence. [plan](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/docs/plans/261009i-the-guide-greets-in-chat-takes-live-and-a-bar-row.md:115), [security-map.md](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/docs/project/security-map.md:93), [routes.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/routes.ts:4781), [chat-tools.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/chat-tools.ts:2093)
+
+2. **P1 — Stored kind alone is insufficient for a fresh Guide Live session.** An empty Guide exists only in the tab, so both token routes currently find no stored thread. The browser must carry `guide` through `LiveApi.start`, both engine request bodies, and the spoken-turn reducer. On the server, the stored kind must be authoritative; a validated browser kind may fill only the no-thread case, and a mismatch should be rejected before spending. `targetOf` preserves one Guide when the exchange is stored, but the token routes’ direct ID lookup does not seed an existing Guide reached through a fresh ID. Test both engines for fresh Guide, stored Guide, mismatched browser/stored kind, create, append, stale fresh-ID collision/tail refusal, and continued refusal of Tutorial, Explore, and Candidates. [plan](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/docs/plans/261009i-the-guide-greets-in-chat-takes-live-and-a-bar-row.md:129), [routes.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/routes.ts:4402), [reduce.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/web/chat/reduce.ts:488), [chat.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/chat.ts:507)
+
+3. **P1 — “Keep this as why you’re reading” is not safe with `savePurpose` as planned.** `usePurpose` reads once, while `savePurpose` performs an unconditional PATCH. A purpose saved in another tab—or later in this tab—can therefore be overwritten by the stale Guide button. A rejected response also does not prove the write failed. Make this an atomic save-if-empty operation that returns either “saved” or the existing purpose; on an ambiguous response, verify with `storedPurpose`. Add a synchronous double-press lock and bind the request with `useMadeFor`. Because a correct atomic operation requires route/store work, it also belongs in the Greg write-up under this run’s constraint; otherwise omit the CTA rather than ship the overwrite race. Tests must cover same-tab save, another-client save immediately before the press, server interleaving, StrictMode/double press, and a response lost after a successful write. [plan](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/docs/plans/261009i-the-guide-greets-in-chat-takes-live-and-a-bar-row.md:99), [purpose.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/web/purpose.ts:24), [purpose.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/web/purpose.ts:136), [routes.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/routes.ts:6530)
+
+4. **P2 — Do not silently truncate the first message into a different reason.** Chat accepts substantially more text than the 600-character purpose field. Offer the CTA only when the complete, storage-normalized message fits; otherwise link to Metadata to write a shorter reason. Test 600/601 characters, whitespace-only input, CRLF normalization, multiline text, and astral Unicode. [plan](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/docs/plans/261009i-the-guide-greets-in-chat-takes-live-and-a-bar-row.md:101), [types.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/types.ts:1598), [pg-shelf.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/store/pg-shelf.ts:366)
+
+5. **P2 — Keep the greeting as an empty-state introduction, not an unstored historical bubble.** A mount-local snapshot prevents an in-place React rewrite, but after reload the apparent “first chat bubble” would be regenerated from the latest title/profile/purpose and change above an old transcript. Persisting a true first bubble adds unjustified v1 complexity. The simplest 80/20 is the current empty-state placement: wait for the purpose read, draw one stable introduction, then remove it after the first turn. This also avoids permanently consuming phone height. Test delayed and out-of-order StrictMode reads, `purposeFailed`, rerenders, first send, and reload after a profile/purpose edit. If it must remain above turns, call and style it as current Guide context rather than conversation history. [plan](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/docs/plans/261009i-the-guide-greets-in-chat-takes-live-and-a-bar-row.md:76), [ChatPanel.tsx](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/web/ChatPanel.tsx:1905), [purpose.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/web/purpose.ts:129)
+
+6. **P2 — Guide history needs voice-specific sanitizing; cost classification does not need changing.** `answerAsSeen` returns Guide answers verbatim, while `liveSeedItems` removes only block IDs. Typed Guide answers can contain `[cmd:…]`, giving the voice model examples of syntax its spoken prompt forbids. Strip command tokens and their now-empty button lines from assistant Guide seed text, then remove block IDs; never alter the reader’s literal text. Test this for both Realtime and GPT-Live while preserving Recall hint behavior. Typed Guide should remain `jobFor("guide") === "chat"`; both Live engines should continue recording `live_conversation`, with explicit regression tests rather than a new Guide cost job. [recall-hint.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/recall-hint.ts:81), [live.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/live.ts:553), [converse.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/converse.ts:146)
+
+7. **P2 — Specify the command row’s capability gate and URL rewrite.** Gate it on both article view and an owner-only capability such as `article.executor?.askGuide`; the catalogue deliberately includes another reader’s article and owner Metadata contexts, so `article !== undefined` or `view === "article"` alone is insufficient. Build a non-generating page row whose helper preserves unrelated state such as `at`, `margin`, and `chatfrom`, removes stale `mode`, `thread`, and `guide`, then sets `mode=chat&guide=1`. Test owner article, experimental-off, archived, visitor, Metadata, old-thread URLs, and Back behavior. [CommandBar.tsx](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/web/CommandBar.tsx:383), [command-proposal.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/web/command-proposal.ts:557), [router.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/web/router.ts:643)
+
+8. **P3 — The greeting table is sensible after tightening attribution, length, and voice.** Quoting the owner’s profile as ordinary React text is safe; do not render it as Markdown or HTML. Prefer “In About you, you wrote: ‘…’” over “your profile says you are,” collapse whitespace, and use the existing Unicode-safe word-boundary clamp for both the profile and the stored purpose. Keep the read-failed title-only arm. The title still needs explicit Reader → ConversationBand → ChatPanel → GuideGreeting plumbing, and the fixed UI prose, reader quotes, and article title should retain their respective visual voices rather than styling the whole greeting as an AI answer. [GuideGreeting.tsx](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/web/GuideGreeting.tsx:51), [Reader.tsx](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/web/reader/Reader.tsx:3220), [title-text.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/title-text.ts:106)
+
+9. **P3 — Help’s alias needs no ranking change, but catalogue acceptance needs pinning.** `Guide` already beats Help for `guide` because a label prefix outranks an alias prefix. Test that Guide is first and Help remains present. Regenerate and verify both generated files, including exact contexts for the Guide row: owner article, experimental-off, and archived; not visitor, Metadata, or no-article. [command-match.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/web/command-match.ts:455), [CommandBar.tsx](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/src/web/CommandBar.tsx:1191), [command-pick-catalogue.test.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbs6qhzv-guide-greets-and-live/tests/command-pick-catalogue.test.ts:286)
+
+The fixed, free greeting and direct Guide command are the right 80/20 for Greg’s first report. Guide Live is also the right product answer to the second, but its safe implementation and the atomic purpose save both require defence-bearing route work, so those portions should be written up for Greg rather than built in this constrained run.
+
+No files were edited and no tests were run. Concurrent Stage 1 edits appeared in the worktree during review; the findings above assess the plan against `HEAD`, not those partial changes.
